  "_note": "HAND-CURATED. The street names people arrive with, the ones the pharmacy names on a drug page never mention. Rendered FIRST under \"Also called\" on the drug page and in the index rows, and joined to the search index so a prefix of any of them finds the page. Every name appears in at least one of the two sources below, and each entry says which; a name with no source does not go in, however common it is (\"fetty\" is the current example - it is in neither, so it lives only in the exact-match slang map in search-intents.json). Names that MISLEAD - a name that says one drug and sells another - belong in name-warnings.json, never here. Short lists on purpose: five to seven a drug, the ones actually said, not the DEA's hundreds.",
